<Guide slug="pos-pricing-setup-vs-monthly" waMessage={WA_MESSAGES.guidePricing} ctaTitle="Get a quote for your business, in writing."
  ctaText="Tell us how many branches and counters you have and what you sell. We will send you the setup, the monthly fee and any hardware, itemised.">
  <p class="draft-banner">Draft — in review</p>
  <p>
    Point of sale prices are hard to compare. One supplier asks for a large amount up front. Another asks for nothing
    up front and a monthly fee. A third says it is free. A fourth takes a small percentage of every sale. They are all
    selling roughly the same thing: a way to sell, count the money and know what happened. So which is cheapest?
  </p>
  <p>The honest answer: it depends on how long you keep it, how many branches you have, and what is included.</p>

  <h2>Compare over three years, not one month</h2>
  <p>
    A point of sale is not a one-month purchase. Most businesses keep theirs for years. So the fair comparison is the
    total over three years, for your number of branches:
  </p>
  <div class="guide-note">
    <p><strong>Setup</strong> (once, for each branch if it is charged per branch)<br />
      + <strong>the monthly fee &times; 36</strong> (&times; the number of branches, if it is per branch)<br />
      + <strong>hardware</strong> you have to buy<br />
      + <strong>anything charged per sale</strong> (a percentage, or a fee per transaction)<br />
      + <strong>extras</strong>: training, support, more points of sale, kitchen screens, installation.</p>
  </div>
  <p>
    Two things move the answer more than anything else. A fee charged <em>per branch</em> doubles when you open a
    second branch. A fee charged <em>per sale</em> grows as you grow: 1% of KES 20,000 a day is KES 200 a day, which is
    about KES 6,000 a month, every month, forever.
  </p>

  <h2>How ZapTill is priced</h2>
  <p>
    ZapTill is paid once per branch for the point of sale — once it is paid, it is yours. The cloud is a single monthly
    fee for the whole business, not per branch, and the first month is free. Nothing is taken per sale: sell more and
    the fee stays the same. A second branch adds its own setup, not a second monthly fee.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because every place is different — branches, counters, kitchen screens — we build the figure around your setup
    rather than print one number. Tell us what you have and we send it back itemised: the setup, the monthly cloud fee
    and any hardware. Analytics, if you want it, is an add-on for the whole business, taken once the cloud has shown you
    what your numbers look like. Hardware is quoted separately, or you bring your own and we check it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Then run the three-year sum above against our quote and against any other you have. <a href="/pricing/">Build your
    quote</a> in a minute, or send us your numbers and we will do it with you.
  </p>

  <h2>What the setup should buy you</h2>
  <p>
    A setup fee is only worth paying if it buys work you would otherwise do yourself, badly, at midnight. Ask what is
    included. A good setup covers:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Installation at your place:</strong> the computers, the printers, the scanner or the pumps, set up and tested.</li>
    <li><strong>Your items loaded for you:</strong> your product list, price list or menu, typed in by someone else.</li>
    <li><strong>Staff roles and PINs,</strong> so each person sees only what they should.</li>
    <li><strong>Training</strong> for cashiers, attendants and managers, on your own products.</li>
    <li><strong>Your logo and colours</strong> on the receipt.</li>
    <li><strong>The first day close, together,</strong> so the first one is right.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>ZapTill's branch setup includes all of these. The full list is on the <a href="/pricing/">quote page</a>.</p>

  <h2>What the monthly fee should buy you</h2>
  <p>
    A monthly fee should pay for something that keeps working for you every month, not for permission to keep using
    what you already paid for. With ZapTill, the points of sale are yours once the setup is paid; the monthly fee is for
    the cloud: every branch on one web dashboard on your phone, a daily summary by email, closing a branch's day from the
    web, partner and accountant logins, and reports to Excel.
  </p>
  <p>
    And if you stop paying? Ask every supplier this. With ZapTill, the points of sale keep selling; what stops is the
    cloud (the dashboard, your phone access, the daily email and syncing) until you pay again, and your sales wait
    safely on the point of sale until then.
  </p>

  <h2>"Free" is a price too</h2>
  <p>A free point of sale can be a good deal. Before you take one, ask:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Is there a fee per sale, or a percentage, or a required payment provider?</li>
    <li>Must I buy their hardware, at their price?</li>
    <li>Who sets it up, and who trains my staff?</li>
    <li>Who do I call when something goes wrong, at what hours, and does it cost extra?</li>
    <li>Does it keep selling with no internet?</li>
    <li>Can I take my data with me if I leave?</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The questions that matter</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>What is the total over three years, for my number of branches?</li>
    <li>Is anything charged per branch, per computer or per sale?</li>
    <li>What exactly does the setup include?</li>
    <li>What does the monthly fee pay for, and what happens if I stop?</li>
    <li>What hardware do I need, and can I use my own?</li>
    <li>When can I get support, and is there a cost?</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    When you have your answers, <a href="/pricing/">build your quote</a> and put ZapTill's figure beside the rest.
  </p>
</Guide>
